section: tools
title: Client tools
about: |
  Rules of the tool that makes the entity, such as the provider, and of the lab. They are out of
  scope for strata-preflight, and they stay in the catalog so that each fault of the live runs has
  a row. A lab row with a check that a command on this machine can answer runs as a cloud check.
rules:
- id: provider-timeout-success
  title: The provider gives exit 0 at its create timeout
  engines:
  - all
  tier: tool
  severity: fail
  status: seen
  what: |
    At its create timeout the provider gives a warning and exit 0 ("Creation complete") while the
    cluster still builds. Gate on `Running`, or run `strata-preflight --watch`.
  fix:
    owner: provider
    text: An error, or an opt-in warning.
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: '#89, #90'
- id: provider-eks-azs
  title: The provider reads cloud_config.azs back on EKS
  engines:
  - eks
  tier: tool
  severity: fail
  status: seen
  what: |
    Provider 0.30.1 does not read `cloud_config.azs` back, and the field forces a new resource:
    each apply replaces the cluster. Found after one apply of 55 minutes.
  fix:
    owner: provider
    text: Read the field.
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: a live run
- id: provider-delete-timeout
  title: A destroy waits until the cluster is gone
  engines:
  - all
  tier: tool
  severity: warn
  status: seen
  what: |
    `tofu destroy` ends with `context deadline exceeded` while Palette still deletes the cluster.
    The provider sends one plain delete and waits for its own deadline. A pipeline sees an error
    with no reason it can read. Read the state of the cluster after the error.
  reproduce:
  - 'strata-preflight --watch cluster:{{ .clusterUid // "<cluster uid>" }}   # the conditions and the events of the delete'
  fix:
    owner: none
  evidence:
  - kind: run
    ref: a live run
    note: the destroy failed with `context deadline exceeded`; a second destroy sent the delete again and completed
